{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Configure node1 as a working passive-only FTP destination using the scanner account from access.txt, confined to the dedicated dropbox.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1 runs an enabled vsftpd service bound to its FTP address. The scanner account uses the staged dropbox as its home and FTP root; chroot is enabled, active-mode transfers are disabled, and access is restricted to the scanner allowlist and node2 network source.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b05b5187863a4f2c","cmd-55bcb2ace4f447e2","cmd-869e0cb644ba4de8","cmd-ddac2b76fa6d4908"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Allow the scanner on node2 to upload and retrieve files over passive FTP, including the supplied sample scan.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 successfully uploaded and retrieved sample-scan.txt using PASV, with matching source and retrieved SHA-256 hashes. Server logs directly record PASV, STOR, RETR, successful upload, and successful download. The workflow also succeeded after both node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2132f691dd6d431e","cmd-e3e0075977d94aba","cmd-1ed054a76f654fb0","cmd-ddac2b76fa6d4908"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Make host files outside the dedicated dropbox inaccessible to the scanner account.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A direct parent-path attempt to retrieve staged access.txt outside the FTP root failed with FTP 550. The observed chroot and local_root configuration place the scanner's FTP view at the dedicated dropbox, and denial persisted after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-576d95addec54deb","cmd-3b2a7f7b3417496d","cmd-83511293f5864289","cmd-ddac2b76fa6d4908"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Ensure anonymous FTP access is unavailable.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Anonymous login was directly rejected with FTP 530 both before and after the restart sequence, consistent with the final anonymous_enable=NO configuration.","evidence_ids":["cmd-576d95addec54deb","cmd-3b2a7f7b3417496d","cmd-83511293f5864289","cmd-ddac2b76fa6d4908"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel, using software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0. Node1 installed signed vsftpd 3.0.5-12.el10 from the RHEL 10 AppStream repository, and final package health was clean.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b05b5187863a4f2c","cmd-9c50c69dc2f34b16","cmd-159110dfcd974c17","cmd-9e5dcbec4eb8487a","cmd-ba3cebc82bbb4ae5","cmd-ddac2b76fa6d4908","cmd-e70383fc899840fa","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutation was identified. The initial failed installation downloaded the needed RPM and led directly to importing its verified vendor key and completing the signed installation, so it was a contributing prerequisite rather than an unrelated experiment. Account, configuration, SELinux, firewall, service, transfer, and reboot mutations all had clear task or mandatory evidence roles; temporary client files were removed. The retained vendor configuration copy is a reasonable rollback artifact, not an abandoned conflicting configuration. Final snapshots show no failed services, healthy package state, no unexplained temporary residue, and only the required node1 FTP listener added.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a2ed43b90a74400f","cmd-159110dfcd974c17","cmd-9e5dcbec4eb8487a","cmd-ba3cebc82bbb4ae5","cmd-35536c1307b044e7","cmd-2132f691dd6d431e","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol was also completed coherently on both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart observation, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity matching the fixed lifecycle cross-check, recovered data/network or service state, and a successful end-to-end FTP workflow after both restarts.","limitations":["The outside-dropbox behavioral test targeted the representative staged path ../access.txt rather than attempting an exhaustive sample of host paths; the observed chroot configuration supplies supporting evidence for the broader confinement conclusion."]}
